    "Presenter uses real lease status and actual surface cache-acquisition result. Fatal refusal releases issuer/registry lease first,marks its private stopped state under the swap lock,wakes all waiting producers and returns before show/surface-drop/queue-retirement. Existing genuine Mach-private C thread-exit adapter ends only this CPU worker. Queued surface references and root service remain retained;no GPU reset/power/stop/release or failed-job retry is introduced.",
    "Ordinary pending work keeps the existing1ms cadence;successful show and normal surface-release path remain. Initial CPU presentation before GPU binding remains allowed under the same registry lease. Future SwapEnd calls observe the stopped latch and return without enqueueing or repeating queue waits.",
